{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"850806376740945952","content":"1. Losing Red ensures that you cannot heal  past 50% of your total hp.\n2.Losing Blue causes you begin petrifying into black and white marble.  Attack rolls against you have advantage.\nThe creature automatically fails Strength and Dexterity Saving Throws.\nThe creature has Resistance to all damage.\nThe creature is immune to poison and disease, although a poison or disease already in its system is suspended, not neutralized.\n3.Losing Green\nCauses you to begin shaking and fumbling.\nWhen you miss on an attack:, you drop your weapon or item in your hand. This includes component pouches and arcane focuses. When in combat, you start every round prone. It will cost you half movement to stand. At the end of your turn you will once again fall prone.\n4.Losing Yellow.\nCauses your body to begin sweating.\nThe creature is overcome with fever and cannot take bonus actions or reactions.\nIt has disadvantage on Strength and Dexterity saving throws and checks and attack rolls that use either ability.\nLosing 3 colors results in a loss of all hp.","created_at":"2021-07-12T03:12:14.330000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"863981050078429204","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
